  "note": "2021-2024 sourced from exchange_calendars 4.13.2, which starts XSAU on 2021-01-03 (backfill; not independently verified): 49 closures (6 named), no early closes, then 12 corrections from Saudi Exchange's own holiday events page (https://www.saudiexchange.sa/wps/portal/saudiexchange/about-saudi-exchange/exchange-media-centre/events, read in full 2026-11-20) and the Royal Order on Founding Day; 12 is over the session limit of 10 by maintainer decision, every one being cited to the exchange's own page. Removed (exchange_calendars closes them; the exchange traded): 2021-02-22: the Royal Order creating Founding Day (22 February, an official holiday) was issued on 27 January 2022 (Saudi Press Agency, https://sp.spa.gov.sa/viewfullstory.php?lang=en&amp=&newsid=2324647), so exchange_calendars backdates it; the exchange's page lists Founding Day from 22/02/2022. 2022-07-13: Eid Al Adha 2022, 'Trading will resume after the holiday on 13/7/2022'. 2023-04-25: Eid Al Fiter 2023, 'Trading will resume after the holiday on 25-04-2023'. 2023-07-02: Eid Al Adha 2023, 'Trading will resume after the holiday on Sunday 02-07-2023'. 2024-04-14 and 2024-04-15: Eid Al Fiter 2024, 'Trading will resume after the holiday on 14/04/2024'. 2024-06-13 and 2024-06-23: Eid Al Adha 2024, 'Trading will discontinue at the end of trading day 13/06/2024' and 'Trading will resume after the holiday on 23/06/2024'. Added (the exchange closed; exchange_calendars trades): 2022-09-22: 'National Day of Saudi Arabia is on 22/9/2022'. 2023-06-25 and 2023-06-26: Eid Al Adha 2023, 'Trading will discontinue at the end of trading day Thursday 22-06-2023'. 2023-09-24: National Day 2023, 'Trading will discontinue at the end of trading day 21-09-2023' and 'Trading will resume after the holiday on 25-09-2023'. All 12 are contradicted_by on the 2021-2024 span. 2010-2020: out of scope (exchange_calendars has no XSAU before 2021; Phase 4h); generation_range and coverage start 2021-01-01. Weekend: the Thursday-Friday to Friday-Saturday change of 2013 is outside the 2021-2029 window; weekend_days has no dated form (Phase 4d backlog item if 2010-2020 is ever backfilled). 2025-2026: exchange_calendars + exchange_publications. Checked 2026-11-20 (4c13). Last published year: the exchange's events page publishes Eid holidays through 2029 'According to the UMM AL-QURA calendar'; 4c-final applied them (re-read 2026-11-21): Eid Al Fiter 2027 'Trading will discontinue at the end of trading day 04/03/2027' / 'Trading will resume after the holiday on 14/03/2027'; Eid Al Adha 2027 13/05/2027 / 23/05/2027; Eid Al Fiter 2028 24/02/2028 / 05/03/2028; Eid Al Adha 2028 02/05/2028 / 10/05/2028; Eid Al Fiter 2029 11/02/2029 / 19/02/2029; Eid Al Adha 2029 19/04/2029 / 29/04/2029. The closed days are the Sunday-Thursday days strictly between each pair (30 days), entered as published (predicted=false). Removed: 'Islamic New Year (predicted)' 2027-06-06 and 2029-05-14 (the exchange lists no Islamic New Year closure; its official holidays are Founding Day, Eid Al Fiter, Eid Al Adha and National Day). Founding Day and National Day 2027-2029 are not on the page yet and stay predicted from the standing rules.",
